WEBVTT

00:30.895 --> 00:32.314
We can do it...

00:33.316 --> 00:34.360
...Victor.

00:38.034 --> 00:42.334
<i>A fierce battle between Unrepair Negator Rip
and Andy's group takes place on the open seas.</i>

00:42.627 --> 00:46.175
<i>The countless blades coming
from Rip's Artifact, Blade Runner,</i>

00:46.175 --> 00:48.138
<i>causes much trouble for Andy and the gang.</i>

00:48.221 --> 00:53.899
<i>But with the combination of four Negator abilities-
Unmove, Untouchable, Undead, and Unluck-</i>

00:53.899 --> 00:56.029
<i>they manage to defeat Rip.</i>

00:56.864 --> 00:59.661
<i>A giant UMA appears at Latla's call.</i>

00:59.661 --> 01:04.462
<i>Latla escapes inside it along with Rip,
leaving with the words, "Rip will definitely not die."</i>

01:04.546 --> 01:08.053
<i>The pair disappears into the ocean along
with the other Negator Hunters.</i>

01:08.178 --> 01:12.645
<i>With Rip defeated, the effects of Unrepair's power
are released, and Fuko's life is spared.</i>

01:13.438 --> 01:17.614
<i>Now that the battle's over,
Chikara feels dumbfounded as the tension washes away</i>

01:17.614 --> 01:20.243
<i>when Fuko asks him if he wants to join the Union.</i>

01:20.703 --> 01:24.043
<i>Chikara is still confused at how
the situation changed at breakneck speed,</i>

01:24.043 --> 01:26.130
<i>so Andy decides to give him
a one-week grace period to decide.</i>

01:26.840 --> 01:29.428
<i>Everyday life, or days of battle?</i>

01:29.846 --> 01:33.436
<i>Chikara's decisions at the crossroads
as a Negator is...</i>

01:45.962 --> 01:48.592
Do you think Chikara will come?

01:49.594 --> 01:50.972
Who knows?

01:51.932 --> 01:56.608
We told 'im to show up at the school gates
at five once he's made up his mind.

01:57.025 --> 01:57.902
Yeah.

01:58.696 --> 02:01.827
Ten minutes left.
If he doesn't come, we're outta here.

02:02.537 --> 02:03.288
Yeah.

02:07.087 --> 02:11.555
If his resolve ain't up to snuff, he's better off not joining.
He'll just wind up dead.

02:12.306 --> 02:16.147
You're right.
Everyone's only got one life to live.

02:18.359 --> 02:21.575
And if you end up dying,
there's no coming back.

02:25.040 --> 02:27.504
Actually, that's not as true as you think.

02:27.837 --> 02:28.631
Ah!

02:29.048 --> 02:33.974
Latla said you guys weren't here,
so I figured you would be.

04:13.926 --> 04:15.470
Unrepair?

04:15.470 --> 04:19.771
You're so small...
Wait, you survived! But how...

04:21.984 --> 04:25.867
Nope, I died all right.
Shot through the heart.

04:27.494 --> 04:28.873
I got beat clean.

04:31.461 --> 04:35.093
Long story short,
I ended up looking like this.

04:36.012 --> 04:38.976
No biggie, though.
I'll apparently be back to normal soon enough.

04:39.268 --> 04:42.650
Then wh-why are you here?
Y-You wanna go, punk?

04:43.151 --> 04:45.113
Nah, today I've got a gif-

04:50.499 --> 04:52.754
Ow!

04:52.754 --> 04:53.506
Hmm?

04:54.674 --> 04:57.054
Oh! There goes a baby tooth!

04:59.100 --> 05:01.020
You're right on time, bud.

05:01.479 --> 05:04.653
I wasn't satisfied with just drillin'
a hole through your heart, ya know.

05:04.986 --> 05:07.534
Hm? What are... oh!

05:07.534 --> 05:09.621
You're mad at me for stabbing the girl, right?

05:10.205 --> 05:12.251
Listen. My bad, my bad!

05:13.671 --> 05:16.969
Then again, didn't she jump in harm's way herself?

05:18.346 --> 05:19.641
Is that my fault?

05:21.477 --> 05:22.772
Hey, your wound doing all right?

05:23.022 --> 05:25.695
Huh? Uh, yeah. Mr. Ni-

05:28.534 --> 05:31.999
Er... I mean, a doctor patched me up.

05:32.249 --> 05:35.422
Gotcha! Good to hear!
Sorry about that!

05:36.048 --> 05:38.512
Okay, see? We've made up now!

05:43.689 --> 05:46.235
I'm only here to give you a gift today!

05:47.614 --> 05:48.699
A gift?

05:49.491 --> 05:50.452
Yeah, this!

05:51.580 --> 05:52.414
A handgun?

05:53.124 --> 05:57.382
I thought I'd give you guys the lowdown...
on what it is we're trying to do.

05:58.426 --> 06:01.474
Never handled an Artifact before, right?

06:38.799 --> 06:40.845
Gaaah!

06:40.845 --> 06:41.555
What?

06:44.978 --> 06:45.938
Fuko!

06:48.610 --> 06:51.282
Andy... what is this?

07:05.978 --> 07:10.821
What the hell is this?
I've touched other Artifacts in the past, but...

07:10.821 --> 07:15.831
It depends on the item.
Different Artifacts funnel different images into your mind.

07:16.625 --> 07:18.921
And the image that particular one produces is pretty rare.

07:19.338 --> 07:22.762
What was that thing-
that big, dark figure?

07:23.012 --> 07:27.229
That's who you're after, right?
The God you're all so set on killing.

07:27.814 --> 07:30.068
No one's beating that thing,
don't you think?

07:30.068 --> 07:35.328
That's why we're going to rule
the world until they come to destroy it.

07:36.163 --> 07:40.380
Even though the end is nigh, eh?
That's gonna be one short rule, bud.

07:41.800 --> 07:43.094
What are you talking about?

07:43.679 --> 07:47.603
We can go to the next step.
Unlike any of you.

07:48.020 --> 07:49.064
What?

07:49.231 --> 07:51.068
<i>Calling all off-mission members!</i>

07:52.279 --> 07:57.164
<i>Roundtable members are currently battling
Negator Hunters in Egypt and China.</i>

07:57.164 --> 08:00.211
EGYPT
<i>We need anyone in the vicinity to provide backup!</i>

08:00.420 --> 08:02.508
Come on!
We don't need any backup!

08:23.299 --> 08:27.975
This world turns because we live upon it as vessels.

08:28.810 --> 08:30.689
So, why are we the only ones who fight?

08:31.398 --> 08:33.654
Why are we the only ones who suffer?

08:34.363 --> 08:38.204
It should be the other way around, right?
Otherwise, it'd be unfair.

08:39.666 --> 08:46.262
We're called Under. In three months,
the world will flip around and become fair.

08:56.533 --> 08:59.162
Well, whaddaya think after seeing that?

09:00.791 --> 09:03.547
Not so hot now, are ya?
Think y'can beat that thing?

09:04.590 --> 09:08.139
Join us, and I'll personally put in
a good word for you two.

09:08.347 --> 09:10.101
Hah!
As if, idiot.

09:10.728 --> 09:12.857
If it exists, that means we can kill it.

09:14.318 --> 09:16.573
You really are a riot.

09:17.282 --> 09:19.996
Then give it your best shot... Union.

09:30.141 --> 09:31.728
And there ya have it.

09:34.066 --> 09:36.320
Let's team up and kill God!

09:36.613 --> 09:37.280
Oh!

09:37.948 --> 09:39.284
Chikara!

09:40.078 --> 09:42.833
Erm, I'm sorry.

09:42.833 --> 09:45.129
You didn't mention that part before.

09:45.380 --> 09:46.758
You decided to come-oh...

09:47.760 --> 09:50.682
S-S-S-Sorry! Never mind!

09:50.849 --> 09:51.768
Chikara?

10:00.243 --> 10:01.788
Wait... where's Mr. Andy?

10:04.251 --> 10:07.591
I know what your skill is.
No way I'd fall for that.

10:08.092 --> 10:09.887
I'm sorry!
Please forgive me!

10:10.430 --> 10:12.350
Let's have a li'l talk.

10:12.350 --> 10:14.730
Yes, sir... don't kill me.

10:15.440 --> 10:18.279
Fuko! We're takin' this somewhere else.

10:18.279 --> 10:18.947
Hmm?

10:22.370 --> 10:26.003
Chikara, are there still folks in your classroom?

10:26.003 --> 10:28.884
No, there's nobody left inside.

10:28.884 --> 10:29.844
Gotcha.

10:30.470 --> 10:34.812
Fuko! Chikara said he left somethin' back in class!
Let's head on in!

10:35.104 --> 10:36.649
Really? Is that okay?

10:37.568 --> 10:42.912
Course not. Throw on your blazer
so no one finds out we're outsiders.

10:57.900 --> 11:00.321
What floor?
What grade are you, Chikara?

11:00.822 --> 11:03.537
The fourth floor.
Oh, and, um, I'm a third-year.

11:03.870 --> 11:07.418
Whaa? You're preparing for college, then!
That's amazing!

11:07.418 --> 11:09.924
Amazing, amazing, a-mazing!

11:09.924 --> 11:12.638
- Amazing, amazing, amazing!
- Uh, it is...? W-Well, thanks.

11:12.721 --> 11:15.602
A-mazing, amazing, amazing!

11:15.936 --> 11:16.980
Wow!

11:21.238 --> 11:23.618
A real classroom!
It's so big!

11:25.539 --> 11:29.630
Whoa! Right where the protagonist
looks outside lost in thought!

11:31.091 --> 11:33.178
Back of the class,
near the window!

11:36.978 --> 11:38.355
Um... Mr. Andy?

11:38.857 --> 11:39.567
What's up?

11:39.984 --> 11:43.032
Oh! Serious talk time.
Sorry about that.

11:43.700 --> 11:47.750
You talked about the world ending.
But when is that exactly?

11:48.585 --> 11:53.553
If the quests proceed as normal,
and we keep up a losing streak, then April.

11:53.553 --> 11:58.730
And if the next penalty we get hit with is the world-ender...
then it'll be January.

12:00.692 --> 12:02.070
Huh? Wait, really?

12:04.659 --> 12:08.833
I have two things that I need to do.

12:10.044 --> 12:11.338
One is to live...

12:12.382 --> 12:13.551
...and the other is to atone.

12:19.062 --> 12:21.149
Can I tell a really bleak story?

12:21.149 --> 12:22.820
Huh? Sure.

12:32.213 --> 12:35.512
I've... killed my parents.

12:52.130 --> 12:54.635
<i>It was back when I was a first-year in middle school.</i>

12:56.556 --> 12:59.311
<i>We were on our way home from a shopping trip.</i>

13:00.313 --> 13:03.737
<i>I offered to carry the bags since they were heavy...</i>

13:05.406 --> 13:08.245
<i>...and made my way across the crosswalk,
ahead of them.</i>

13:09.331 --> 13:10.542
Come on, hurry!

13:16.596 --> 13:19.309
Hm? What's wrong with you two?

13:20.687 --> 13:22.440
<i>I didn't realize it at the time.</i>

13:22.983 --> 13:26.658
<i>That it was my fault my mom
and dad couldn't move.</i>

13:27.325 --> 13:33.087
<i>Then, before I knew it, a truck barreled toward them
from just out of view, its driver asleep.</i>

13:35.676 --> 13:38.180
<i>Right when I tried to run towards them...</i>

13:49.202 --> 13:50.664
My dad died instantly.

13:51.456 --> 13:58.137
My mom suffered serious injuries.
She tried her very best, but passed a week later.

13:59.849 --> 14:06.361
<i>My mom's final words were,
"Be someone who can take action for others."</i>

14:10.036 --> 14:16.048
It was a while after that when I realized
my ability caused that accident.

14:19.220 --> 14:25.274
I thought about ending my life multiple times.
But every time I did, I saw my parents' faces.

14:32.038 --> 14:36.254
It made me wonder what they would want me to do now.

14:36.881 --> 14:41.181
They'd likely tell me it was okay
to die if things were too hard for me.

14:43.728 --> 14:48.863
But there's no way they'd want that!
It's your own child!

14:50.826 --> 14:54.165
Of course they'd want me to live!

14:57.422 --> 15:02.432
That's why... I need to keep on living.

15:02.725 --> 15:06.691
I don't have to impress anybody.
If I just keep on surviving...

15:07.568 --> 15:10.322
...that maybe, in some small way...
it'd help make me a better son.

15:12.118 --> 15:14.957
I kept telling myself that.
That's how I've been living.

15:19.675 --> 15:25.645
<i>But then the mafia caught me,
and threw me in a cage.</i>

15:25.771 --> 15:27.106
<i>Just when I was about to be killed...</i>

15:31.156 --> 15:32.701
I met the two of you.

15:34.412 --> 15:41.343
Not only did you save me,
you also taught me that my ability can help others.

15:47.940 --> 15:49.902
I've been searching all this time.

15:51.488 --> 15:55.204
A way, outside of simply living,
to make my amends.

15:58.670 --> 16:02.636
I know that I freaked out earlier,
but I won't run away anymore.

16:04.890 --> 16:07.436
So, please allow me...
to be part of the team!

16:08.606 --> 16:09.274
Hmm?

16:09.482 --> 16:14.660
Hey, Chikara!
Club's wrapped up! Let's head home!

16:15.494 --> 16:17.081
- Hmm?
- Hmm?

16:19.210 --> 16:20.004
Hmm?

16:20.755 --> 16:23.928
Uh, so, who's the old dude repeating
the same grade for the tenth time?

16:25.014 --> 16:26.266
Come on, Ryo!

16:27.936 --> 16:30.316
Looks like you really did go too far!

16:32.779 --> 16:36.954
And who is she? That's not our school's blazer.
You in trouble with them?

16:36.954 --> 16:39.960
Uh, no, no.
You've got it all wrong.

16:39.960 --> 16:41.338
There's something totally off about this.

16:41.338 --> 16:43.801
It might look that way, but...

16:43.801 --> 16:46.557
- Also, the look of their eyes-
- Oh, no, wait, no...

16:51.483 --> 16:53.655
How long ya gonna keep laughing?

16:53.655 --> 16:59.374
No, no, no, no!
I can't take it anymore!

17:14.571 --> 17:16.659
By the way, I got some big news.

17:15.659 --> 17:16.744
Huh? What's that?

17:17.203 --> 17:19.625
I'm headed to Antai University on
a basketball scholarship!

17:19.834 --> 17:21.671
Wow, seriously?
That's great!

17:21.671 --> 17:25.887
You betcha! Now I don't have
to hear my mom's bellyaching!

17:25.887 --> 17:27.975
Dang, Ryo.
You really are something!

17:32.108 --> 17:34.070
You really are amazing, Ryo.

17:34.070 --> 17:37.076
Well, yeah.
I guess I am something, huh?

17:37.745 --> 17:38.622
Chikara.

17:38.622 --> 17:39.289
- Huh?
- Hmm?

17:39.874 --> 17:41.753
It's time. Let's go.

17:42.588 --> 17:43.715
Oh. Right.

18:01.793 --> 18:04.005
Hey, Chikara. What are you do-

18:06.594 --> 18:09.182
Hey, Ryo.
Thank you for everything.

18:10.059 --> 18:12.773
School was so much fun thanks to you.

18:13.190 --> 18:15.737
<i>What...? My body won't move.</i>

18:16.781 --> 18:22.250
If... if we manage to kill God...
let's graduate together!

18:25.423 --> 18:28.137
Whoa! I can move!
Dammit...

18:28.555 --> 18:29.222
Chikara!

18:30.892 --> 18:32.103
Hey, Chikara!

18:34.232 --> 18:36.027
Hold on! What's going on?

18:50.974 --> 18:53.605
I knew it!
They were trouble!

18:59.533 --> 19:02.246
I'd like the memory thing done.

19:02.831 --> 19:04.042
You sure?

19:04.042 --> 19:07.841
Yes. It makes things safer
for everyone, right?

19:08.091 --> 19:08.760
Yeah.

19:12.266 --> 19:13.185
Then I'd like it done.

19:15.607 --> 19:17.068
Hit it, Nico.

19:17.193 --> 19:18.530
Roger that.

19:23.080 --> 19:24.332
Hey, you jerks! Wait!

19:24.625 --> 19:26.211
Where do you think you're taking Chikara?

19:26.587 --> 19:27.881
Hang tight, I'm coming to save...

19:28.883 --> 19:29.593
...you?

19:33.016 --> 19:34.728
Huh? Oh.

19:35.145 --> 19:38.528
Crap, I left my bag back in class!

19:38.528 --> 19:40.447
What a pain!

19:42.703 --> 19:47.253
Hmm... but why am I all out of breath?

19:57.398 --> 19:58.108
Get us outta here.

20:08.838 --> 20:09.673
Andy.

20:10.717 --> 20:11.384
Yeah?

20:11.969 --> 20:14.975
I want to beat God.

20:15.810 --> 20:21.947
So that Chikara can go to school again.
So that the world doesn't come to an end.

20:24.160 --> 20:25.162
That's why...

20:26.247 --> 20:31.592
Will you teach me... how to fight?

20:37.061 --> 20:37.979
Sure.

20:45.452 --> 20:46.956
September 16.

20:48.125 --> 20:53.135
Andy and Fuko succeeded in persuading
the 11th Negator to join the Union.

20:58.270 --> 21:05.618
As a result, a level eight information blackout
was conducted on anyone with memories of Chikara Shigeno.

21:07.748 --> 21:08.750
Addendum:

21:09.960 --> 21:17.684
A special training regimen was put underway
per Fuko Izumo and Chikara Shigeno's requests.

21:20.481 --> 21:21.274
And so...

21:21.274 --> 21:22.736
2020

21:22.736 --> 21:24.238
DECEMBER 1ST

21:24.238 --> 21:25.742
UNION FACILITY,
ROUNDTABLE ROOM

21:42.483 --> 21:43.820
We're all assembled, yes?

21:44.822 --> 21:46.784
You may proceed, Apocalypse.

21:47.326 --> 21:50.040
Quests, open!

22:01.020 --> 22:06.030
TO BE CONTINUED

23:36.044 --> 23:36.795
PREVIEW

23:37.046 --> 23:40.762
<i>Are untouchable warmths
of the world all illusions?</i>

23:40.845 --> 23:44.561
<i>Within a darkness that never will connect,
it finally arises.</i>

23:44.686 --> 23:48.359
<i>Next episode of Undead Unluck,
Episode 16-Revolution.</i>

23:48.611 --> 23:50.489
<i>In search of the greatest death ever.</i>
